    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\n2 Bedroom First floor apartment c. 80 sqm with large glazed corner window and balcony area. In Longford's most desirable residential location.\n\nThis very spacious apartment is on the first floor in a block of just 8 apartments. The apartment is presented in good condition. The open plan kitchen / living & dining area features a gas fireplace and built in kitchen units. There is an integrated dishwasher, gas oven & hob, and a washer dryer. \n\nThere is a glazed corner wall area around the dining area and there is access to a small balcony area. This looks out onto agricultural lands behind the apartment block. There are south & west facing aspects meaning the living area is bright throughout the afternoon. Combined with the extra high ceilings the living area has a bright and airy feel.\n\nThe bedrooms are both double sized with built in slide wardrobes. The main bedroom has an ensuite shower room and there is a separate bathroom. \n\nThe apartment is fully furnished and includes all appliances and comes with vacant possession. It is an ideal small home with remote working possibilities with high speed fibre and cable gigabit broadband available.\n\n\nServices\n• Mains Water and Sewerage, \n• Gas fired central heating (Calor LPG) new condensing boiler installed in March 2025.\n• Cablecom Gigabit broadband available\n• Refuse bins for scheme\n\n\nSaint Albans:\nApproached by a tree lined avenue and surrounded by mature planted grounds that are constantly maintained by the management company. The development consists of all private town houses and apartments. \n\nThe service charge for 2025 is 1525 p.a (reduced 1325 for prompt payment) to include Block insurance, refuse bins, security gates and common areas maintenance.\n\n\nLocation:\nSituated behind the fine period houses of the Battery Road. This area has long been regarded as Longford's most desirable address.\nThe town centre is only a short walk, as are local amenities such as the tennis and rugby club, the Mall River Park & sports complex etc. The main N4 Dublin-Sligo Road is within a minutes' drive.\n\n\nEircode: N39 A218 \nGPS: 53.7338, -7.8039"
      },
